oriander leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped fresh coriander leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 20, "raw": "¼ cup cider vinegar (approximately)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "cider vinegar (approximately)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 21, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place beans in a bowl, cover with cold water to a depth of 2 inches, add thyme and allow to soak at least 4 hours or overnight."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat a heavy 2- to 3-quart casserole. Add cumin seeds and stir until they begin to dance around and smell toasty. Remove seeds and set aside."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add oil. Saute the onion, carrot and bacon for 10 minutes, until the bacon is golden. Add jalapeno pepper, garlic and cumin seeds and cook a few minutes longer."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Preheat oven to 300 degrees."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Drain beans and add to the casserole along with canned and fresh tomatoes, maple syrup, brown sugar, bay leaf, orange rind and crushed peppercorns. Stir in all but 1 tablespoon of the coriander. Add 2 cups cold water. Cover and bring to slow simmer."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Place beans in oven and cook for 1 hour. Add vinegar and season to taste with salt. Cook 1 hour longer, until liquid has been absorbed but the beans are still moist."}, {"position": 7, "text": "Adjust seasonings. Add salt and pepper and up to 2 more tablespoons cider vinegar if desired. Garnish with reserved coriander."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 456.6, "protein_g": 19.6, "carbohydrates_g": 58.3, "fat_g": 17.3, "saturated_fat_g": 5.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 24.9, "