{"slug": "bibimbap-style-soba-noodle-salad", "nyt_id": 759867054, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/759867054-bibimbap-style-soba-noodle-salad", "name": "Bibimbap-Style Soba Noodle Salad", "author": "Hetty Lui McKinnon", "description": "In this meal-prep friendly twist on bibimbap, the kaleidoscopic Korean mixed rice dish, simple vegetable sides seasoned with sesame oil or soy sauce (called namul) are served with nutty soba noodles, and lavishly tossed in a spicy-sweet gochujang dressing. Blanching is a great way to lock in the vibrant hues, distinct textures and fresh flavors of vegetables. While it’s a very simple process, it does require some precision to ensure optimal results: Season the blanching water generously, cook the vegetables briefly, and, after cooking, expel as much water as possible. The different vegetables and noodles are prepared separately, so they can be easily packed away individually, ready for assembling a quick weekday lunch or a future dinner. Use whatever vegetables you have on hand. (Carrots, daikon, broccoli, kale and corn would also work well.) For extra heartiness, top with a fried egg.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 10, "cook_minutes": 25, "total_minutes": 35, "raw": {"total": "35 min", "prep": "PT0H10M", "cook": "PT0H25M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Salt and pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "8 ounces/4 cups soy or mung bean sprouts", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "ounces/4 cups soy or mung bean sprouts", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "5 teaspoons toasted sesame oil, divided", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "toasted sesame oil", "preparation": "divided", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 medium zucchini (about 1 pound), thinly sliced into disks", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium zucchini (about 1 pound)", "preparation": "thinly sliced into disks", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 teaspoons gochugaru (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "gochugaru", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 6, "raw": "6 ounces fresh shiitake mushrooms, stemmed and sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "fresh shiitake mushrooms", "preparation": "stemmed and sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "10 ounces baby spinach", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "baby spinach", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "8 ounces soba noodles", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "soba noodles", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 scallions, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Toasted white sesame seeds, for serving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "toasted white sesame seeds", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "¼ cup gochujang paste", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "gochujang paste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "2 tablespoons soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 teaspoons rice vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "rice vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "2 teaspoons sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "1 teaspoon granulated sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "granulated sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a large pot of salted water to the boil. Add the bean sprouts and blanch for 2 minutes. Using a large spider skimmer or tongs, lift the sprouts out of the water and drain in a colander. (Keep the water boiling.) Drain the bean sprouts well, pressing out as much water as possible and then transfer to a small bowl. Add 1 teaspoon of sesame oil, season with salt and pepper and toss to coat."}, {"position": 2, "text": "To the same boiling water, add the zucchini and blanch until tender, 2 to 3 minutes. Using a large spider skimmer or tongs, lift the zucchini out of the water and place into the colander, pressing out as much water as possible. Transfer to a medium bowl and add 1 teaspoon of sesame oil and the gochugaru (if using); season with salt and toss to coat."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Repeat this same process for the mushrooms, blanching for 2 minutes, then transferring to the colander and pressing out excess water. Place them in a bowl and season with 1 teaspoon of soy sauce and 1 teaspoon of sesame oil; toss to coat."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add the spinach to the water a few handfuls at a time, adding more as it wilts, pressing it down to submerge it completely. Cook until wilted, which should only take about 30 seconds, and then transfer to the colander, squeezing out the excess water. Transfer to a small bowl, add 1 teaspoon of sesame oil and season with salt and toss to coat."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Finally, add the soba noodles to the water and cook according to package instructions until al dente. Drain the noodles, discarding the water, and rinse the noodles under cold water. Transfer to a medium bowl, add 1 teaspoon of sesame oil and season with salt."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Make the gochujang dressing: Place the gochujang paste, soy sauce, rice vinegar, sesame oil and sugar in a medium bowl. Loosen with 2 tablespoons of water and whisk to combine."}, {"position": 7, "text": "To serve, divide the noodles among four bowls (or lunch boxes/containers) and top each with a bundle of bean sprouts, zucchini, mushrooms and spinach. Drizzle the gochujang sauce over each bowl and top with scallions and sesame seeds."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 388.7, "protein_g": 17.8, "carbohydrates_g": 62.3, "fat_g": 11.5, "saturated_fat_g": 1.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 1676.0, "fiber_g": 6.5, "sugar_g": 8.8, "unsaturated_fat_g": 8.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["vegan", "vegetarian", "dairy-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["lunch", "school lunch", "dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["gochujang", "sesame oil", "soba noodle", "zucchini", "shiitake", "noodles", "kid-friendly", "quick", "stovetop", "great leftovers", "spinach", "weeknight", "budget"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2025/10/08/multimedia/hlm-bibimbap-style-soba-noodle-salad-mzqt/hlm-bibimbap-style-soba-noodle-salad-mzqt-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 106}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2025-10-08", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:04:42.735193+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "big-batch-grilled-vegetables", "nyt_id": 10865, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10865-big-batch-grilled-vegetables", "name": "Big-Batch Grilled Vegetables", "author": "Marian Burros", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Fourteen servings", "min": 14, "max": 14, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 45, "raw": {"total": "45 minutes, plus overnight refrigeration"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 cups white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 cups olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "4 cloves garlic, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "6 large pieces lemon rind, about ½ cup", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large pieces lemon rind", "preparation": "about ½ cup", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "6 large pieces orange rind, about ½ cup", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large pieces orange rind", "preparation": "about ½ cup", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup minced rosemary, plus additional sprigs for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "minced rosemary", "preparation": "plus additional sprigs for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Freshly ground black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "7 Japanese eggplants, halved lengthwise", "group": null, "quantity": 7.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "japanese eggplants", "preparation": "halved lengthwise", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "7 medium zucchini, halved lengthwise", "group": null, "quantity": 7.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium zucchini", "preparation": "halved lengthwise", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "14 large red, yellow or orange bell peppers (any combination), quartered", "group": null, "quantity": 14.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large red", "preparation": "yellow or orange bell peppers (any combination), quartered", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Thyme sprigs for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "thyme sprigs for garnish", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Combine the wine, oil, garlic, lemon and orange rinds, rosemary and pepper, and divide between 2 large nonaluminum roasting pans."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Arrange the vegetables in the pans and toss with the marinade. Refrigerate overnight. Stir the vegetables occasionally so that all of them are coated."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Grill the vegetables at a distance of 6 to 8 inches from the hot coals until tender, turning often and brushing with the marinade. The eggplant will cook in about 20 minutes, the peppers and zucchini in 10 minutes. As the vegetables are cooked, arrange them on serving platters. Cut the eggplant and zucchini in quarters crosswise. Decorate with the sprigs of rosemary and thyme."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 432.0, "protein_g": 5.7, "carbohydrates_g": 31.1, "fat_g": 32.2, "saturated_fat_g": 4.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 21.9, "fiber_g": 13.6, "sugar_g": 17.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 26.4, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["dairy-free", "gluten-free", "vegan", "vegetarian"], "course": ["side dis