{"slug": "bitter-herbs-salad", "nyt_id": 12360, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12360-bitter-herbs-salad", "name": "Bitter Herbs Salad", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "Bitter herbs – the maror – are part of the Seder ritual, symbolizing the bitterness of slavery experienced by the Jews in Egypt. Endive, romaine and chicory (for which I’ve substituted radicchio) are present on many Sephardic ritual platters, but often they also appear in salads served with the meal. This can be served as a separate course or as a side dish.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 hearts of romaine lettuce", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "hearts of romaine lettuce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 small head radicchio", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small head radicchio", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 Belgian endives", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "belgian endives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 ½ cups arugula or watercress, washed and dried", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "arugula or watercress", "preparation": "washed and dried", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 rib celery, preferably from the heart, sliced very thin", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "rib celery", "preparation": "preferably from the heart, sliced very thin", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 scallions, chopped (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": true}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ cup chopped flat-leaf parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped flat-leaf parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ cup chopped fresh dill", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped fresh dill", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped fresh mint (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh mint", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 small garlic clove", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small garlic clove", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "3 tablespoons freshly squeezed lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "freshly squeezed lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "½ cup extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Wash and dry the romaine lettuce leaves and break into medium pieces. Separate the radicchio leaves and cut into medium pieces. Rinse and dry the endives and slice crosswise about ¾ inch thick. Toss together all of the greens, the celery and the scallions in a large salad bowl and sprinkle the herbs over the top."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Skin the garlic clove, cut in half and remove green shoots. Place in a mortar and pestle with a generous pinch of salt and mash to a paste. Work in the lemon juice and then the olive oil. Taste and adjust salt. Tra